hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1084","Chapter on the prohibition of killing envoys, 1122 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man - meaning the envoy of Musaylimah: Were it not that you are an envoy, I would have killed you."
